      "summary": "This document is an Adverse Event Report Form (Form SYN-AE-01) generated for testing purposes. The report concerns an 84-year-old male patient with a relevant medical history of stage 4 chronic kidney disease. The patient's weight is not stated in the document. The reporting individual is Dr Sofia Marchetti, a physician based in Italy. The suspect product involved is Renalix, administered orally at a dose of 10 mg daily. Treatment with Renalix was initiated on 18 December 2025. On 05 January 2026, the patient experienced severe hyperkalaemia and cardiac arrhythmia. The event outcome was fatal, classifying the reaction as serious due to death. Laboratory test tables highlight a high serum potassium level of 6.8 mmol/L and a low serum sodium level of 134 mmol/L. The laboratory results also show elevated creatinine at 212 umol/L, elevated urea at 18.4 mmol/L, and a reduced eGFR of 28 mL/min. Patient weight, concomitant medications, and drug stop date are not stated in the report. Action taken with the suspect drug and dechallenge or rechallenge information are not stated. The exact date of death and any autopsy results are also not stated in the document.",
